:: OC Kade Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
You are moving through the slightly crowded hallways trying to rub sleep from your eyes when a boy in front of you catches your attention. You’re not sure what it is that catches your attention, since he seems pretty unremarkable from first glance. His unkempt black hair, the way he holds a textbook to his chest like a shield, or how he drags his feet every so slightly as he walks. You’ve never spoken to him before but have seen him around school once or twice you think. He isn’t in any of your classes, though you assume you must be in the same grade, due to his small size, unless he skipped a grade or two. You at first figure this must just be one of those moments where something ordinary in your everyday life catches your attention, <span style="Color: Yellow">but maybe you noticing him was your brain subtly warning you of what was about to happen.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightCoral">Trip! <br>
<br>
An upperclassman sticks his foot out in front of the boy, sending the short lad flying to the ground! He lands in a heap, textbook sliding against the lockers as his bag falls to the ground and its contents spill out. He lands hard, face hitting the floor with his butt firmly in the air in a pretty pathetic position. The boy groans in discomfort as the upperclassman and his friend laughs.</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Kade",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Uniform",
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Eyes: "Sad",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Watch it, nerd! You almost scuffed up my new sneakers!”</span> He says with a devious smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Maybe I’ll have to bill your daddy. Probably use to it since his son’s such a fucking safety hazard.”</span> The boy’s words are harsh, coming from the confidence a few years and a couple inches over someone else gives you. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry…”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">The boy says softly, avoiding eye contact as he begins to collect his papers. The boy doesn’t even try to fight back, just taking their bullying with hardly a word.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice1">
	<<link "Help him pick up his papers<br>">>
	<<replace"#choice1">>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You walk over and bend down to help the boy pick up his scattered papers, feeling bad for him.</span> He looks at you nervously for a second before quickly glancing away. The upperclassmen laugh, shouting out <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What? Is this your boyfriend?”</span> and other teasing remarks. You just ignore them, wanting to help the kid without bringing undue attention to either of you. <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "OC Kade",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: Yellow">Then something happens. As they walk away triumphantly, one of the boys reaches down and slaps the victim’s rear end. Just a simple hard tap, a final act of humiliation. But for a brief moment this seems to light a fire under the boy.</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">His eyes sharpen as he glares at the bully with a fury that almost unnerves you. His fists clench, crumpling the paper in his hands. He looks, briefly, like he was about to attack the kid.</span> But then it vanishes, his eyes turn back timid and he takes a deep breath, returning to picking up his papers. The change is so sudden you have to do a double take. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Th- thank you…”</span> The boy says nervously as you hand him the rest of his papers. You ask him if he’s alright and he nods. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m fine. They didn’t hurt me, or anything, so it’s fine.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">The boy looks awkwardly at the floor for a second before giving you a shy, but genuine, smile of gratitude. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“My- my name is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>, if you didn’t know… I’ve seen you in the hallways, but we haven’t spoken or anything, so figured you probably don’t know.”</span> The boy seems friendly, if a little shy. You return his smile, reaching out and shaking the boy’s hand. Your response seems to calm his nerves a little.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "OC Kade",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“N- nice to meet you. I- I should get to class, but… thanks again!”</span> He gives you one last smile before hurrying off. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span> <span style="Color: Pink"> actually seems pretty happy to have gotten the chance to introduce himself to you.</span> <br>
        <<set $OCKadeSocial to 0>>
        <<set $OCKadeSocialRank to 0>>
        <<socialChange "Kade" 5 1>>
        <<set $InActiveQuests.delete("Kade: Introduction")>>
        <<set $ActiveQuests.push("Kade: Introduction")>>
        <br>
        <<if $Location.Name == "School South Hallway">>
        [[Continue|School South Hallway]] 
        <<elseif $Location.Name == "School East Hallway">>
        [[Continue|School East Hallway]]
        <<else>>
        [[Continue|School West Hallway]]
        <</if>>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Laugh and slap his rear<br>">>
	<<replace"#choice1">>
        <span style="Color: Pink">You begin to chuckle at the boy’s misfortune. The fact that he didn’t even try to fight back and just let those guys walk all over him is hilarious. You swear some people prefer the role of victim. You walk over, intentionally stepping on his papers, and decide to add one last humiliation as you reach down and give him a hard slap on the rear.</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">But the instant you do that, something changes…</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "OC Kade",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Uniform",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightCoral">The boy’s head snaps to you, his eyes sharpening to a glare that actually makes a pit appear in your stomach. You instantly feel your fight or flight instincts kick in, as if the single look sent a danger warning shockwave up your body. You freeze like a deer in the headlights, maybe for just a second, before the boy’s face returns to normal.</span> The timid, shy look he had a second ago returns as he stares at the ground and tries to avoid your eyes. The upperclassmen laugh, praising your slap, but your body is still full of adrenaline until the boy rushes down the hall, scattered papers in hand. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Poor <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kade</span>.”</span> You hear a nearby student whisper, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“They only pick on him because they know he won’t fight back.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Not every rich kid can be popular.”</span> Another responds with a shrug, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Think it makes them feel better about not being rich. Whatever. Not our problem.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: Yellow">As the gathered crowd disperses, you find yourself both intrigued and a little scared by what you saw. But you guess it was just a brief moment where his anger at being picked on exploded out. Oh well.</span> <br>
        <<set $OCKadeSocial to 0>>
        <<set $OCKadeSocialRank to 0>>
        <<socialChange "Kade" -10 1>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
